{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UP84vjb3dq1nP3bfsbwfWQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — vla-ssd\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: CoRL 2026\n5\t- Deadline: Abstract May 26, Paper May 29\n6\t- Format: 8 pages + references\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n9\t\n10\t1. **Vision Encoder Dominance**: VLA 中 action-relevant 表征结构由 frozen vision encoder（SigLIP）决定。SigLIP+projector 的 RSA 与 action structure 的相关性（ρ=0.615）远高于完整 VLA（ρ≈0.488）和 standalone vision model（DINOv2 ρ=0.388）。\n11\t2. **LLM Degrades Action Alignment**: LLM processing 降低而非增强 action-relevant 几何结构（0.615→0.488）。这一 degradation 在 trained/untrained、with/without instruction 四种条件下一致发生。\n12\t3. **Training and Instruction Invariance**: VLA task-specific fine-tuning（Δ<0.01）和 instruction input（Δ<0.005）均不显著改变 LLM hidden state 中的 action-relevant 表征结构。2×2 matrix（training × instruction）四格收敛于 0.48-0.49。\n13\t\n14\t## Story Spine\n15\t\n16\t- **Problem**: VLAs 通过 fine-tuning LLM on robot data 实现 impressive performance，但 action-relevant 表征从何而来？业界隐性假设 fine-tuning 注入 new representational knowledge，但无系统性验证。\n17\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Grant et al. 2026 从 behavioral level 发现 visual pathway dominates，但未做 representational decomposition。无人测量过 VLA 各组件（vision encoder / projector / LLM）对 action-relevant 表征结构的独立贡献。\n18\t- **Our framing**: 首次对 VLA 进行系统性 representational analysis——7 种 probing 方法 × 2 benchmarks × 组件级分解，定量揭示 action-relevant 结构的来源。发现 LLM 不仅不贡献，反而 degrades vision encoder 提供的 action alignment。\n19\t- **Headline result**: \"SigLIP+projector representations achieve RSA ρ=0.615 with action structure, while the full VLA only achieves ρ≈0.488 regardless of training or instruction — the LLM degrades rather than enhances action-relevant representations.\"\n20\t\n21\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n22\t\n23\t### C1: 单一 VLA 架构（OpenVLA）泛化性\n24\t- **应对**: Scope 明确限定为 \"OpenVLA-class architecture\"。OpenVLA 是最广泛使用的开源 VLA 之一，findings 对该架构族直接适用。Discussion 中讨论扩展到其他架构的预期。\n25\t- **实验**: 无需额外实验，Limitations 明确标注。\n26\t\n27\t### C2: SigLIP vs DINOv2 pretraining confound\n28\t- **问题**: SigLIP 是 image-text contrastive pretrained，DINOv2 是 self-supervised。RSA gap 可能来自 language-aware pretraining 而非纯 vision encoder 质量。\n29\t- **应对**: 这个 confound 实际上 **强化** 我们的 story——如果 gap 来自 SigLIP 的 vision-language pretraining，说明 pretraining 阶段的 language grounding 远比 task-specific fine-tuning 重要。Discussion 正面讨论此 confound 并将其转化为 insight。\n30\t- **实验**: P2 可补 CLIP vs DINOv2 对比，但非 blocking。\n31\t\n32\t### C3: LLM degradation 机制不清\n33\t- **问题**: 为什么 LLM 降低 action alignment？\n34\t- **应对**: LLM 对 representation 做 next-token prediction 优化的变换，这与保持 action-relevant geometric structure 目标不同。Projector bottleneck（D026 发现 SigLIP+projector frozen）约束了信息通路。Discussion 讨论 information bottleneck 解释。\n35\t- **实验**: Per-layer RSA degradation curve 作为 P1 supplementary evidence。\n36\t\n37\t### C4: Grant 2026 checkpoint 差异\n38\t- **问题**: Grant 用 OFT fine-tuned，我们用 standard fine-tuning checkpoint。\n39\t- **应对**: 我们用 standard fine-tuning 是更强的测试——如果完全不同的 LLM 权重（random init vs pretrained+finetuned，cos_sim≈0.2）都不改变表征，OFT 更不会。Related Work 明确区分。\n40\t\n41\t### C5: Practical implications 不够\n42\t- **问题**: 发现了问题，然后呢？\n43\t- **应对**: 三个可操作建议：(1) 投资 vision encoder pretraining 质量比 LLM fine-tuning 更重要；(2) representation-based downstream tasks 应直接使用 projector output 而非 LLM hidden states；(3) VLA 架构设计应关注减少 LLM 对 visual structure 的 degradation。\n44\t\n45\t## Key Evidence Inventory\n46\t\n47\t| Evidence | Claim | Status |\n48\t|----------|-------|--------|\n49\t| SigLIP+Projector RSA=0.615 | C1, C2 | ✅ Done |\n50\t| Full VLA RSA ≈ 0.488 (4 conditions) | C2, C3 | ✅ Done |\n51\t| DINO RSA=0.388 | C1 | ✅ Done |\n52\t| 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks: trained ≈ untrained | C3 | ✅ Done |\n53\t| Instruction ablation Δ=0.004 | C3 | ✅ Done |\n54\t| 2×2 matrix Bootstrap CI includes 0 | C3 | ✅ Done |\n55\t| Output head analysis: SigLIP+projector frozen | C1, C2 | ✅ Done |\n56\t| Per-layer RSA degradation curve | C2 | 🔄 P1 supplementary |\n57\t| Random instruction control | C3 | 📋 P1 planned |\n58\t\n59\t## Literature Positioning\n60\t\n61\t- **Grant et al. 2026**: Behavioral level \"visual pathway dominates\" → 我们 representational level 确认 + 定量组件分解\n62\t- **Fang 2025**: \"Fine-tuning erodes VLM reasoning\" → 我们发现 LLM step 本身（不只是 fine-tuning）就降低 visual structure\n63\t- **Hou 2026 (LangGap) / Fei 2025 (LIBERO-Plus)**: \"VLAs ignore language instructions\" → 我们从 representation level 解释 why：instruction text 对表征结构无实质影响\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f463e76-0b11-4e2b-97f3-bb7dd01573c8","uuid":"c2611e9d-0a50-4c7d-902b-c61110cc2950","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:38:45.928Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T222933/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — vla-ssd\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: CoRL 2026\n- Deadline: Abstract May 26, Paper May 29\n- Format: 8 pages + references\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Vision Encoder Dominance**: VLA 中 action-relevant 表征结构由 frozen vision encoder（SigLIP）决定。SigLIP+projector 的 RSA 与 action structure 的相关性（ρ=0.615）远高于完整 VLA（ρ≈0.488）和 standalone vision model（DINOv2 ρ=0.388）。\n2. **LLM Degrades Action Alignment**: LLM processing 降低而非增强 action-relevant 几何结构（0.615→0.488）。这一 degradation 在 trained/untrained、with/without instruction 四种条件下一致发生。\n3. **Training and Instruction Invariance**: VLA task-specific fine-tuning（Δ<0.01）和 instruction input（Δ<0.005）均不显著改变 LLM hidden state 中的 action-relevant 表征结构。2×2 matrix（training × instruction）四格收敛于 0.48-0.49。\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: VLAs 通过 fine-tuning LLM on robot data 实现 impressive performance，但 action-relevant 表征从何而来？业界隐性假设 fine-tuning 注入 new representational knowledge，但无系统性验证。\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Grant et al. 2026 从 behavioral level 发现 visual pathway dominates，但未做 representational decomposition。无人测量过 VLA 各组件（vision encoder / projector / LLM）对 action-relevant 表征结构的独立贡献。\n- **Our framing**: 首次对 VLA 进行系统性 representational analysis——7 种 probing 方法 × 2 benchmarks × 组件级分解，定量揭示 action-relevant 结构的来源。发现 LLM 不仅不贡献，反而 degrades vision encoder 提供的 action alignment。\n- **Headline result**: \"SigLIP+projector representations achieve RSA ρ=0.615 with action structure, while the full VLA only achieves ρ≈0.488 regardless of training or instruction — the LLM degrades rather than enhances action-relevant representations.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n\n### C1: 单一 VLA 架构（OpenVLA）泛化性\n- **应对**: Scope 明确限定为 \"OpenVLA-class architecture\"。OpenVLA 是最广泛使用的开源 VLA 之一，findings 对该架构族直接适用。Discussion 中讨论扩展到其他架构的预期。\n- **实验**: 无需额外实验，Limitations 明确标注。\n\n### C2: SigLIP vs DINOv2 pretraining confound\n- **问题**: SigLIP 是 image-text contrastive pretrained，DINOv2 是 self-supervised。RSA gap 可能来自 language-aware pretraining 而非纯 vision encoder 质量。\n- **应对**: 这个 confound 实际上 **强化** 我们的 story——如果 gap 来自 SigLIP 的 vision-language pretraining，说明 pretraining 阶段的 language grounding 远比 task-specific fine-tuning 重要。Discussion 正面讨论此 confound 并将其转化为 insight。\n- **实验**: P2 可补 CLIP vs DINOv2 对比，但非 blocking。\n\n### C3: LLM degradation 机制不清\n- **问题**: 为什么 LLM 降低 action alignment？\n- **应对**: LLM 对 representation 做 next-token prediction 优化的变换，这与保持 action-relevant geometric structure 目标不同。Projector bottleneck（D026 发现 SigLIP+projector frozen）约束了信息通路。Discussion 讨论 information bottleneck 解释。\n- **实验**: Per-layer RSA degradation curve 作为 P1 supplementary evidence。\n\n### C4: Grant 2026 checkpoint 差异\n- **问题**: Grant 用 OFT fine-tuned，我们用 standard fine-tuning checkpoint。\n- **应对**: 我们用 standard fine-tuning 是更强的测试——如果完全不同的 LLM 权重（random init vs pretrained+finetuned，cos_sim≈0.2）都不改变表征，OFT 更不会。Related Work 明确区分。\n\n### C5: Practical implications 不够\n- **问题**: 发现了问题，然后呢？\n- **应对**: 三个可操作建议：(1) 投资 vision encoder pretraining 质量比 LLM fine-tuning 更重要；(2) representation-based downstream tasks 应直接使用 projector output 而非 LLM hidden states；(3) VLA 架构设计应关注减少 LLM 对 visual structure 的 degradation。\n\n## Key Evidence Inventory\n\n| Evidence | Claim | Status |\n|----------|-------|--------|\n| SigLIP+Projector RSA=0.615 | C1, C2 | ✅ Done |\n| Full VLA RSA ≈ 0.488 (4 conditions) | C2, C3 | ✅ Done |\n| DINO RSA=0.388 | C1 | ✅ Done |\n| 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks: trained ≈ untrained | C3 | ✅ Done |\n| Instruction ablation Δ=0.004 | C3 | ✅ Done |\n| 2×2 matrix Bootstrap CI includes 0 | C3 | ✅ Done |\n| Output head analysis: SigLIP+projector frozen | C1, C2 | ✅ Done |\n| Per-layer RSA degradation curve | C2 | 🔄 P1 supplementary |\n| Random instruction control | C3 | 📋 P1 planned |\n\n## Literature Positioning\n\n- **Grant et al. 2026**: Behavioral level \"visual pathway dominates\" → 我们 representational level 确认 + 定量组件分解\n- **Fang 2025**: \"Fine-tuning erodes VLM reasoning\" → 我们发现 LLM step 本身（不只是 fine-tuning）就降低 visual structure\n- **Hou 2026 (LangGap) / Fei 2025 (LIBERO-Plus)**: \"VLAs ignore language instructions\" → 我们从 representation level 解释 why：instruction text 对表征结构无实质影响\n","numLines":64,"startLine":1,"totalLines":64}}}
